<title>GERMANY: Asian vegetable oils imports seen rising - Oil World.</title>
<headline>Asian vegetable oils imports seen rising - Oil World.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Imports of vegetable oils and animals fats in six key Asian countries are forecast to rise to 5.67 million tonnes in Oct/June 1996/97, from 4.80 million in the same 95/96 period, Oil World newsletter said.</p>
<p>The forecast comprised 17 commodities but a clear lead was taken by palm oil and sunflower oil, the independent publication said.</p>
<p>China and India would be responsible for half the expected growth in overall demand by the group of six countries, which also included Pakistan, Bangladesh, Iran and Iraq.</p>
<p>Chinese imports in the nine months were forecast at 2.57 million tonnes after 2.32 million a year earlier.</p>
<p>India's were pegged at 1.10 million tonnes (690,000) while Pakistan's were seen unchanged at 990,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>Imports by Bangladesh were put at 340,000 tonnes (220,000 previously) while combined imports by Iran and Iraq were forecast at 670,000 tonnes (580,000).</p>
<p>-Vera Eckert, Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
</text>
